---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { u } from "../lib/url.js";
import sources from "../data/sources.json";
const groups = [...new Set(sources.map(s => s.g))];
---
<Base title="Sources">
  <h1>Sources</h1>
  <p class="lede">What has been read, where it is, and what it actually established. Fourteen sources
  across four countries' worth of record-keeping.</p>

  {groups.map(g => (
    <section>
      <h2>{g}</h2>
      {sources.filter(s => s.g === g).map(s => (
        <div class="card" style="margin:.9rem 0">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:.35rem">{s.t}</h3>
          <p style="margin:.2rem 0 .5rem">{s.d}</p>
          {s.id !== "—" ? <p class="small mono" style="margin:.2rem 0">{s.id}</p> : null}
          <p class="small" style="margin:.35rem 0 0"><strong>What it established:</strong> {s.use}</p>
        </div>
      ))}
    </section>
  ))}

  <h2>Currency</h2>
  <p>Every source above was consulted on <strong>7 September 2026</strong>. Nothing here is quoted from
  memory or from another family tree: each claim on this site traces to one of these, or is marked
  <span class="chip">inferred</span> and reasoned out in the open.</p>
  <p>The twenty-six record citations carried over from the family's own MyHeritage tree are listed in
  full, with their archival references, in <span class="mono">data/record-citations.tsv</span> in the
  repository. The forty-three register entries behind the households are in
  <span class="mono">data/households.tsv</span>.</p>

  <h2>What has not been read</h2>
  <p>Set out in full, with the reason in each case, on <a href={u("/open-questions")}>Open questions</a>.
  The short version: the two Brisbane immigration files, the Archdiocese of Benevento church records,
  the Arienzo marriage supplements, and everything on Antenati.</p>
</Base>
